From 97202d54833a62235045413407bd9d628186aa75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 21:20:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [SDL3-DOS] dos: patch 0133 -- one-time CRTC offset register
 dump

Piggybacked on SDL_HINT_DOS_BANK_CHUNK_PROBE's existing activation (no
new hint) -- a one-time, read-only read of the standard VGA CRTC Offset
Register (index 0x13, via 0x3D4/0x3D5), logged alongside fb_state's own
vram_pitch (BIOS-declared BytesPerScanLine).

Confirmed by reading SDL_dosmodes.c directly: this backend's mode-set
path never calls VBE function 4F06 (Set/Get Logical Scan Line Length)
and never reads this register back -- BytesPerScanLine/vram_pitch is
trusted from VBE GetModeInfo with zero independent verification against
the actual hardware register that governs display scanout stride.

Motivated by a real-hardware Mach64 investigation (dossage/Passage):
a careful pixel-diff characterization (not a glance) of the corrupted
region found distinct vertical color bands with sharp edges and
structured-but-misplaced content -- the classic visual signature of a
scanout stride mismatch, not noise or a stale frame (ruled out
explicitly: the region changes MORE than actively-animated content
elsewhere, so it isn't frozen). Explicitly a SEPARATE hypothesis from
SDL/0128-0132's CPU-bus dosmemput/dosmemget readback puzzle -- the CRTC
governs display scanout, architecturally independent from the banked
window's read/write bus semantics, so this and the GR04/05 Read Mode
theory could both be real and unrelated to each other.

Deliberately does not attempt the *2 -> logical-width conversion as a
final answer -- vendor-specific extension bits for higher-resolution
modes are chip-specific and not decoded here; logs the raw register so
the multiplier can be confirmed once real data is in hand rather than
guessed at.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
index c391a2585..05ef458af 100644
--- a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
+++ b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
@@ -1266,6 +1266,45 @@ static void dos_bank_chunk_probe_resolve(void)
             "GR08(BitMask)=0x%02x",
             gr[0], gr[1], (gr[1] >> 3) & 1, gr[1] & 3, gr[2], gr[3]);
     }
+
+    // SDL/0133: one-time CRTC Offset Register (index 0x13) read, via the
+    // standard color-CRTC index/data port pair 0x3D4/0x3D5 present on
+    // every VGA-compatible chip. This is "detected" ground truth for the
+    // scanout stride the DISPLAY HARDWARE actually uses, independent of
+    // whatever BytesPerScanLine the VBE BIOS's GetModeInfo call
+    // ("declared", per this hub's harness-invariants.md) reported at
+    // mode-set time -- this backend's mode-set path (SDL_dosmodes.c)
+    // never calls VBE function 4F06 (Set/Get Logical Scan Line Length)
+    // and never reads this register back, so BytesPerScanLine/vram_pitch
+    // is trusted with no independent verification against the hardware
+    // that actually matters for what's displayed. A stride mismatch here
+    // is architecturally UNRELATED to SDL/0128-0132's CPU-bus
+    // dosmemput/dosmemget readback investigation (the CRTC governs
+    // display scanout, not the CPU's read/write bus into VRAM through
+    // the banked window) -- this tests a second, independent hypothesis
+    // for the ORIGINAL visual corruption, not the readback puzzle.
+    //
+    // Standard VGA convention is actual_stride_bytes = CRTC[0x13] * 2 in
+    // byte-addressing mode (the common case); some chips select a
+    // different multiplier or extend the register's range via
+    // vendor-specific bits elsewhere (e.g. CRTC[0x17] bit 6, or an
+    // extended-offset bit on some SVGA chips) -- deliberately NOT decoded
+    // here since that's chip-specific and would be guessing. Log the raw
+    // register plus the *2 interpretation next to vram_pitch so a human
+    // (or a future patch, once the right multiplier for this specific
+    // chip is confirmed) can compare them directly.
+    {
+        outportb(0x3D4, 0x13);
+        const Uint8 crtc13 = inportb(0x3D5);
+        dos_port_dbg_log(
+            "sdl: SDL/0133 CRTC-OFFSET-DUMP (read-only, ports 0x3D4/0x3D5) "
+            "CRTC13(Offset)=0x%02x (*2=%u bytes, standard VGA byte-mode "
+            "convention -- may need a different multiplier on this chip) "
+            "vs vram_pitch=%d (BIOS-declared BytesPerScanLine, never "
+            "independently verified against this register by this "
+            "backend's mode-set path)",
+            crtc13, (unsigned)crtc13 * 2, fb_state.vram_pitch);
+    }
 }
 
 static void dos_bank_chunk_probe_maybe_log(const Uint8 *src, Uint32 src_off,
